{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QRogersPentagonArchimedean","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QRogersPentagonArchimedean","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rogersAlpha_bounded_under_convergence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rogersAlpha_bounded_under_convergence","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L219-L230","doc":"The product u·v factors through the pentagon: if u, v < 1 then\nα(u, v) and β(u, v) are also < 1 in absolute value (provided\nthe denominator 1 - uv is non-zero).  Stated as a positivity\nbound for the well-definedness of the recursive pentagon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instRogersCorrectionLeadingOrderH4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instRogersCorrectionLeadingOrderH4","kind":"instance","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L212-L217","doc":"Default instance: the leading h-order is 4, recorded as a\ntype-level fact. Downstream theorems consume this via\n`[RogersCorrectionLeadingOrderH4]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RogersCorrectionLeadingOrderH4.leading_h_order_eq_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RogersCorrectionLeadingOrderH4.leading_h_order_eq_four","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L210-L210","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RogersCorrectionLeadingOrderH4.leading_h_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RogersCorrectionLeadingOrderH4.leading_h_order","kind":"def","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L209-L209","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RogersCorrectionLeadingOrderH4.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RogersCorrectionLeadingOrderH4.mk","kind":"ctor","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L208-L208","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RogersCorrectionLeadingOrderH4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RogersCorrectionLeadingOrderH4","kind":"class","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L205-L210","doc":"Conditional-class statement: the Rogers correction's leading\nnon-trivial h-order is h⁴. Encoded as a Prop-valued field for\ninstance-style consumption. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rogersAlphaBeta_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rogersAlphaBeta_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L183-L186","doc":"At u = v = 0, both α and β are 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rogersAlpha_eq_beta_at_diagonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rogersAlpha_eq_beta_at_diagonal","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L177-L181","doc":"At u = v, the Rogers α and β substitutions coincide. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.borromeanH4BestSpec_misses_target_by_more_than_1pct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.borromeanH4BestSpec_misses_target_by_more_than_1pct","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L157-L173","doc":"**Witnessed negative — the Pachner→h⁴ chain does NOT close via a natural\n`(u,v)` specialisation** (`computations/pentagon-to-borromean-h4-probe.witness.json`,\nstatus `exploratory`).  The post-τ pentagon residual's h⁴ coefficient\n(`c4_residual`) at every natural Borromean specialisation has\n`matches_borromean_target_within_1pct = false`; the best match\n(`half_h_squared`, `borromeanH4BestSpecCoeff ≈ 2.488e-7`) is **positive**\nwhile the Borromean Markov-trace target `−3/4` is negative — wrong sign,\n~100 % relative miss.  So `conj:pachner-pentagon-borromean` is genuinely\nun-exhibited (`QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean` carries no\ninstance).  Concretely the absolute miss exceeds the 1 % tolerance band:\n`c4 − (−3/4) > (1/100)·(3/4)`.\n\n(Replaces a prior `4.0e-5 < 1.0e-3` placeholder that asserted a q-log²\n\"improvement\" not present in any committed witness, citing the wrong file.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.borromeanH4BestSpecCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.borromeanH4BestSpecCoeff","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L152-L155","doc":"Best-match specialisation's pentagon-residual h⁴ coefficient\n(`half_h_squared`), from the Pachner→h⁴ probe.\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] computations/pentagon-to-borromean-h4-probe.witness.json ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qRogersAnalyticContinuation_qEqOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qRogersAnalyticContinuation_qEqOne","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L126-L150","doc":"**Model with the predicate read as its own witness.**\n`q_rogers_holds_at` is *defined* to be `fun _u _v q => q = 1`,\ndiscarding both `u` and `v`, so the conjectural field\n`q_rogers_holds_classical : ∀ u v, q_rogers_holds_at u v 1` unfolds\nto `1 = 1` and closes by `rfl` for every configuration.  Nothing\nabout the Rogers five-term identity, convergence of `(u, v)`, or\nthe q-log² correction is encoded; the field is satisfied by\nchoosing the predicate to be the equation the field asserts.\n\nThe real classical-limit content in this file is\n`rogersLogCorrection_factored` and `rogersLogCorrection_at_zero`,\nwhich compute; this model touches neither.  Note also\n`DilogPentagonAssociator`'s description of this class as the place\nwhere \"the `Li₂` five-term stays an honest conjecture class\" — that\nis the intended state, and it is what the demotion restores.\n\n**A `def`, not an `instance`, since 2026-08-24**, and given a name:\nit was anonymous, so resolution supplied it under the generated\nname `instQRogersAnalyticContinuation`.  Nothing in the corpus\ntakes `[QRogersAnalyticContinuation]`.\n\nCallers name it: `letI := qRogersAnalyticContinuation_qEqOne`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QRogersAnalyticContinuation.q_rogers_holds_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QRogersAnalyticContinuation.q_rogers_holds_classical","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L124-L124","doc":"At q = 1, the classical Rogers identity holds for all\nconvergent (u, v). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QRogersAnalyticContinuation.q_rogers_holds_at","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QRogersAnalyticContinuation.q_rogers_holds_at","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L121-L121","doc":"The (u, v, q) configurations where the q-Rogers identity\nis established. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QRogersAnalyticContinuation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QRogersAnalyticContinuation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L118-L118","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QRogersAnalyticContinuation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QRogersAnalyticContinuation","kind":"class","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L108-L124","doc":"The q-Rogers analytic-continuation conjecture as a Lean class.\n\nAt q = 1, the classical Rogers identity holds (provable via\nreal-log arithmetic + polylogarithm formalisation pending in\nMathlib).  At q ≠ 1, the q-log² Rogers correction is the\nproposed extension; the conjectural content is encoded in the\nclass field.\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b-cond, downstream theorems consume the class\nvia [Instance]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-rogers-pentagon-archimedean","label":"prop:q-rogers-pentagon-archimedean","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-rogers-pentagon-archimedean.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rogersLogCorrection_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rogersLogCorrection_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L102-L106","doc":"The degenerate pentagon vertex: the Rogers correction vanishes at\n`u = v = 0` (both log arguments are `1`; `Real.log_one`).  Complements\n`rogersAlphaBeta_at_zero`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rogersLogCorrection_eq_log_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rogersLogCorrection_eq_log_sub","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L91-L100","doc":"**Mathlib filler.** The Rogers `log²` correction in additive-log form\n(`Real.log_div`) — the algebraic skeleton of the five-term identity's\ncorrection term; the full identity awaits a Mathlib `Li₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rogersLogCorrection_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rogersLogCorrection_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L72-L78","doc":"The Rogers correction is symmetric in u ↔ v.\n**Verified** unconditionally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rogersLogCorrection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rogersLogCorrection","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L62-L70","doc":"The classical log² Rogers correction term:\n  log((1-u)/(1-uv)) · log((1-v)/(1-uv))\n\nAt q = 1 this is the exact correction term in the\nRogers-Abel five-term identity (Lewin 1981 §1.6).\nDefined via Real.log (no specialised polylogarithm needed). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rogersAlphaBeta_complement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rogersAlphaBeta_complement","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L52-L60","doc":"The α-β complement identity: (1 - α) · (1 - β) = (1-u)(1-v)/(1-uv).\n**Verified** unconditionally by direct algebra (requires\n1 - u·v ≠ 0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rogersAlpha_beta_symmetry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rogersAlpha_beta_symmetry","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L45-L50","doc":"The Rogers-substitution symmetry: α(u, v) = β(v, u).\n**Verified** unconditionally by direct algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rogersBeta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rogersBeta","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L40-L43","doc":"Rogers's β-substitution: β(u, v) = v(1-u)/(1-uv).\nSymmetric to rogersAlpha in u ↔ v. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rogersAlpha","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rogersAlpha","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QRogersPentagonArchimedean.lean#L34-L38","doc":"Rogers's α-substitution: α(u, v) = u(1-v)/(1-uv).\nDefined unconditionally; users specialise to convergence\ninputs |u|, |v|, |uv| < 1 where needed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}